1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,030
Not all knowledge lives in your site's content index.

2
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:09,880
Some of it is in a search index that another system maintains, or

3
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:11,656
in a database table.

4
00:00:11,656 --> 00:00:17,940
This video shows data sources that read Elasticsearch, Azure AI Search and PostgreSQL.

5
00:00:22,540 --> 00:00:27,879
A search index or a database that another team keeps up to date is knowledge already.

6
00:00:27,879 --> 00:00:31,400
Copying it into your site by hand would only go stale.

7
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:36,146
An external data source reads it where it is, splits it into passages,

8
00:00:36,146 --> 00:00:38,460
and keeps your knowledge base in step.

9
00:00:39,210 --> 00:00:44,887
Elasticsearch, Azure AI Search and PostgreSQL each have their own source type.

10
00:00:44,887 --> 00:00:49,820
Everything after the connection is the same as for any data source.

11
00:00:54,020 --> 00:00:57,392
The connection settings tell the site where to read:

12
00:00:57,392 --> 00:01:01,055
the index and its address, or the database and its table.

13
00:01:01,055 --> 00:01:03,380
Your technical team provides them.

14
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:08,417
The destination is a knowledge base index of your site, the same one

15
00:01:08,417 --> 00:01:11,430
that every data source stores its passages in.

16
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:17,198
The field mapping names the fields that hold the content, the title and the key.

17
00:01:17,198 --> 00:01:22,450
Here you type the names, because the site cannot list the fields of a remote source.

18
00:01:26,655 --> 00:01:33,665
Open Artificial Intelligence, Data Sources, click Add Data Source, and click Add on Elasticsearch.

19
00:01:34,117 --> 00:01:37,571
Enter a Name, and the Index name, which is the name of the

20
00:01:37,571 --> 00:01:39,297
index on the other server.

21
00:01:39,751 --> 00:01:42,005
Choose the Environment type.

22
00:01:42,005 --> 00:01:45,320
Self-managed asks for the Elasticsearch URL.

23
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:49,763
Choose the Authentication type your technical team gives you:

24
00:01:49,763 --> 00:01:53,211
none, a user name and password, or an API key.

25
00:01:53,665 --> 00:01:57,964
Choose the Destination index, the knowledge base index of your site.

26
00:01:57,964 --> 00:02:00,405
It cannot be changed after you save.

27
00:02:00,858 --> 00:02:05,257
In Field Mapping, type the Content field, the Title field and the Key

28
00:02:05,257 --> 00:02:08,248
field, as they are named in the remote index.

29
00:02:08,709 --> 00:02:09,700
Click Save.

30
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:15,119
The data source reads the remote index, and fills its knowledge base in the background.

31
00:02:19,295 --> 00:02:23,765
Choose the data source on a profile, on the Knowledge tab, exactly as

32
00:02:23,765 --> 00:02:25,315
for any data source.

33
00:02:25,770 --> 00:02:28,969
Then ask a question that the remote notes answer:

34
00:02:28,969 --> 00:02:30,830
how do I reset the router?

35
00:02:31,388 --> 00:02:36,908
The assistant answers from the remote index, and the numbered source shows the note it used.

36
00:02:41,112 --> 00:02:45,676
An Azure AI Search data source asks for a Name, the Index name,

37
00:02:45,676 --> 00:02:48,652
and the Endpoint of the search service.

38
00:02:49,106 --> 00:02:54,941
Authentication offers an API key, which is stored securely and never shown again,

39
00:02:54,941 --> 00:02:59,166
or an identity, with the Client ID of a managed identity.

40
00:02:59,619 --> 00:03:03,799
The Destination index and the Field Mapping work as before.

41
00:03:03,799 --> 00:03:07,849
Azure AI Search does not support the Filter of a profile.

42
00:03:12,049 --> 00:03:17,883
A PostgreSQL data source asks for a Name, and the Connection string of the database.

43
00:03:17,883 --> 00:03:22,419
The connection string is stored securely, and never shown again.

44
00:03:22,873 --> 00:03:25,433
The Table name is the table to read.

45
00:03:25,433 --> 00:03:29,945
In Field Mapping, the content, title and key fields are the names of

46
00:03:29,945 --> 00:03:31,653
columns of that table.

47
00:03:35,853 --> 00:03:40,843
A search index that a product team already maintains, for support answers.

48
00:03:41,593 --> 00:03:47,163
An Azure AI Search index of manuals, shared by several applications.

49
00:03:47,913 --> 00:03:52,613
A database table of articles or notes, read without a copy.

50
00:03:54,613 --> 00:03:58,888
Point a data source at the index or table where the knowledge already

51
00:03:58,888 --> 00:04:02,080
lives, map its fields, and choose it on a profile.

52
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:03,563
Thanks for watching.

